  "slug": "rna-decodes-a5dd",
  "summary": "Spatial transcriptomic and scRNA-seq methods now model scale, geometry, and host tissue explicitly rather than leaving them implicit.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is inference conditioned on spatial scale, tissue geometry, or host environment. multiScaleAC makes scale dependence explicit by scoring ligand-receptor cell-cell interactions as a function of Gaussian kernel bandwidth. SFinx models spatially varying pathway activity through spatial fingerprints and spatial functional data analysis. CurvSeq and CurvSee integrate gland curvature with spatial transcriptomic and protein imaging data in prostate cancer. The paired scRNA-seq study of colorectal tumors and liver metastases addresses host dependence through a different design, identifying genes consistently adapting to host liver tissue. Across these items, context is treated as a modeled variable, though the metastasis study reaches it via paired sampling rather than spatial modeling.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-26"
}
